===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₁rewdʰ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|red|id=red}}, from {{inh|en|ang|rēad}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*raud}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*raudaz}} from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*h₁rowdʰós}}, from the root {{m|ine-pro|*h₁rewdʰ-}}.

{{rel-top|Cognates}}
See also {{cog|fy|read}}, {{cog|nds|root}}, {{m|nds|rod}}, {{cog|nl|rood}}, {{cog|de|rot}}, {{cog|da|-}} and {{cog|nb|rød}}, {{cog|nn|raud}}; also {{cog|cy|rhudd}}, {{cog|la|ruber}}, {{m|la|rufus}}, {{cog|xto|rtär}}, {{cog|txb|ratre}}, {{cog|grc|ἐρυθρός}}, {{cog|sq|pruth||redhead}}, [[Russian]] [[рудый|''ру́дый'']] (rúdyj) ("red", "redhaired"). {{cog|cs|rudý}}, {{cog|lt|raúdas}}, [[Serbo-Croatian]] [[riđ|''riđ'']] ("reddish", "red"), {{cog|ae|𐬭𐬀𐬊𐬌𐬛𐬌𐬙𐬀}}, {{cog|sa|रुधिर|tr=rudhirá||red, bloody}}. {{rel-bottom}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|redder|more}}

# Having {{l|en|red#Noun}} as its [[color]].
#: {{ux|en|The girl wore a '''red''' skirt.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 4-2|II|iv|passage=Your colour, I warrant you, is as '''red''' as any rose.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author={{w|J.R.R. Tolkien}}|title={{w|The Fellowship of the Ring}}|chapter=I: A Long-Expected Party|series={{w|The Lord of the Rings}}|isbn=9780345339706|date=29 July 1954|seriesvolume=1|passage= The flowers glowed '''red''' and golden: snapdragons and sunflowers, and [[nasturtians]] trailing all over the turf walls and peeping in at the round windows. }}
# {{lb|en|of hair}} Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; [[ginger]].
#: ''Her hair had '''red''' highlights.''
# {{lb|en|of the skin}} With a red hue due to [[embarrassment]] or [[sunburn]].
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1982|author=Douglas Adams|authorlink=Douglas Adams|title=Life, the Universe and Everything|page=23|text=[T]he sun was shining on a happy crowd. It shone on white hats and '''red''' faces. It shone on ice lollies and melted them.}}
# {{lb|en|card games|of a card}} Of the [[hearts]] or [[diamonds]] suits. Compare {{m|en|black||of the spades or clubs suits}}
#: ''I got two '''red''' queens, and he got one of the black queens.''
# {{lb|en|politics|often|capitalized}} Supportive of, related to, or dominated by a political party or movement represented by the color red:
## [[left-wing|Left-wing]] parties and movements, chiefly [[socialist]] or [[communist]], including the U.K. [[Labour]] party and the [[w:Social Democratic Party of Germany|Social Democratic Party]] of [[Germany]].
##* "Only Nixon could go to China" was the refrain of conventional wisdom during Richard Nixon’s 1972 official visit to Mao Tse-tung’s regime. Nixon’s anti-communist credentials, however dubious, provided useful camouflage as he opened diplomatic relations with '''Red''' China and made breathtaking concessions that an undisguised liberal couldn’t get away with. [https://web.archive.org/web/20061114093022/http://www.thenewamerican.com/tna/1998/vo14no16/vo14no16_dragon.htm]
##: ''the '''red'''-black grand coalition in Germany''
## {{lb|en|US politics}} The U.S. [[Republican Party]]. {{defdate|21st c.}}
##: ''a '''red''' state''
##: ''a '''red''' Congress''
# {{lb|en|chiefly|derogatory|offensive}} [[Amerind]]; relating to [[Amerindian]]s or [[First Nations]]
#* '''1994''', Soundgarden, ''Spoonman''
#*: All my friends are Indians / All my friends are brown and '''red'''
# {{lb|en|astronomy}} Of the lower-frequency region of the (typically visible) part of the electromagnetic spectrum which is relevant in the specific observation.
# {{lb|en|particle physics}} Having a [[color charge]] of red.

